Two decided questions, written down rather than left as standing hesitations.
Docs + changelog only; no behaviour change.

ADR-0055 — LINKER ACTIVATION TIGHTENING IS REFUSED, ON MEASUREMENT.

The number this was being judged on was wrong, and the instrument was ours:
readback.py filters silence as `edges_emitted == 0`, IGNORING nodes_emitted —
the conflation pass_silence.py calls "the headline's original error repeated one
level down". Recomputed strictly over the 9-repo cohort (2,538,624 ms total):

  loose filter (the circulated 4.5%)   39,048 ms  1.54%
  strict, all passes                   21,192 ms  0.83%
  strict, Framework-subcategory, of 25  4,216 ms  0.166%  <- the whole prize

The circulated 4.5% was the loose filter on the cohort EXCLUDING pretix, which
carries 90% of its pass time. 10 of the 13 Framework candidates already cost
ZERO ms — they read framework-enriched symbols and are de-facto gated already.

Decisive argument is neither cost nor risk appetite: a paired bakeoff
differential proves no loss only WHERE DETECTION SUCCEEDED, while the risk is
detection failing on a repo the cohort lacks — which yields an empty baseline
and reads clean. THE CHANGE CANNOT BE VALIDATED AGAINST ITS OWN FAILURE MODE.

Also settled: a gated-off linker produces NO AnalysisRun, so the loss cannot be
disclosed today (blocking precondition, not a property of the tree); and
prerequisite_absent is not the landing value for a closed gate.

Criterion of four conditions — ZERO of 25 qualify. Three triggers, each fireable
from ordinary bakeoff output with no gating work.

ADR-0056 — THREE OF THE FOUR PRODUCERLESS VALUES ARE MIS-HOSTED.

dependency_unavailable / backend_disabled / pass_crashed describe a pass that
DID NOT RUN, which never produces an AnalysisRun — and silence_reason is a field
ON AnalysisRun. No carrier exists to stamp. Their home is
limits.skipped_passes[].reason, beside their free-text twins.

prerequisite_absent is the only well-hosted one and is SECOND-ORDER: the
propagation of the other three downstream, so it cannot be stamped correctly
until they have structured producers. That ordering was never written down.

The producer INV-hujog asks for is refused on measurement: 98.94% of 229,541
skip records are `no files matched`, so an unsatisfied depends_on conjunct
nearly always means the repo lacks that language — State A, a correct no-op —
and prerequisite_absent is declared as State C, the ordering defect.

The value is KEPT, not deprecated: 40 of 69 conjuncts are all grammar-gated, so
a JS+Rust repo on a machine without tree-sitter-language-pack produces a real
State C. The "unmeasurable here" objection fails both halves — 60 circom records
prove the state has occurred on this machine unnoticed, and the blindness is a
venv, not a law. Acceptance test named, runnable before any producer work.

INV-hujog's unfireable trigger is restated onto records that already exist and
have already fired 2,443 times. Work filed as WI-jijor (falsification detector,
independent) -> WI-dukoh (skip_reason_code, blocks) -> WI-dabup (the producer).

Both file as ADRs rather than docs/audits/: audit_findings._REGISTRIES binds
exactly three registry-backed axes and VALID_VERDICTS is closed, so neither can
be expressed there (ADR-0054 records the rule).

CORRECTION CARRIED IN 0056: the supporting instance that a gate "would have
